From d75c106ca021eb803d765b6248774ada8a6905e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:57:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): hold archive marker custody across peer windows
 [daveey]

Address independent review of PR4059 at d5614d916e83845bb2414e4afaef76bf9e9a35de.
The win query parameter identifies a window type, not unique ownership. A
fresh peer or second secondary renderer could report a still-live archive
cancelled, delete its restart marker, then leave that archive running.

Hold an origin-wide Web Lock for each queued attempt before persisting its
marker. Drop reporters acquire the same lock non-blockingly, so they only
retire orphan markers after Chromium releases a destroyed renderer's locks.
No safety verdict or mutation is replayed; restart still uses the explicit
visible drop-note branch. Disposal releases custody, including storage
failure, and late acquisition cannot persist an already disposed intent.
Unsupported custody fails visibly instead of pretending persistence works.

Proof: three initial cross-window/orphan tests RED on reviewed head.
Additional real-preflight six-minute outage plus peer mount RED there too.
All 42 action test files / 369 cases GREEN with the fix; renderer tsc and
applicable eslint pass. Test setup supplies the dependency-free nonblocking
Web Locks subset missing from jsdom. This is simulated renderer coverage,
not laptop native/live acceptance. Live gate remains OPEN/UNPROVEN.

The PR's five-whys and transport investigation remain unchanged: exact
Mac-to-hub transport cause UNDETERMINED, no transport fix in this change.
